Package: simling
Title: Simulated Linguistic Data for Teaching Statistics
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Massimiliano", "Canzi", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           email = "massimiliano.canzi@uni-konstanz.de",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-6124-0321"))
Description: Simulated data sets for teaching statistics to linguists, from
    phonetics, psycholinguistics, syntax, morphology, semantics and
    pragmatics, conversation analysis, corpus linguistics, sociolinguistics,
    dialectology, second language research, language acquisition, historical
    linguistics and typology, and from languages including German, Italian,
    Mandarin, Cantonese and Korean. Responses include continuous measures,
    reaction times, binary and multi-category outcomes, ratings, counts,
    eye-tracking and EEG measures and time series, in data sets from 18 to
    over 20,000 rows. Each data set comes with the code that generated it, so
    the true effects are known.
